.\" -*- mode: troff; coding: utf-8 -*-
.TH QLCHROOT 8
.SH NAME
qlchroot \- enter a Qwaderton Linux chroot with virtual filesystems mounted
.SH DESCRIPTION
.LP
\fBqlchroot\fR runs a command inside a directory prepared as a system
root, bind-mounting the virtual filesystems first and unmounting them
afterwards: \fI/dev\fR, \fI/dev/pts\fR, \fI/proc\fR, \fI/sys\fR,
\fI/run\fR (as tmpfs), and \fI/sys/firmware/efi/efivars\fR on EFI
systems. The target's \fI/etc/resolv.conf\fR is temporarily replaced
with the host's so name resolution works inside the chroot; the
original is restored on exit.
.LP
The command runs with a clean environment (\fIenv \-i\fR) and a minimal
\fBPATH\fR. If no command is given, \fI/bin/sh\fR is started
interactively.
.LP
All mounts are torn down on exit, including when the command is
interrupted (SIGINT/SIGTERM); stale mounts from aborted sessions are
unmounted before new ones are added.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-k\fR
Keep mounts after the command exits (for inspection or nested chroots).
.TP
\fI<dir>\fR
Directory to chroot into.
.TP
\fI[command...]\fR
Command to run inside the chroot (default: \fI/bin/sh\fR).

.SH EXAMPLES
.LP
Enter a chroot for maintenance:
.RS
\f(CRqlchroot /mnt\fR
.RE
.LP
Run a single command and keep the mounts for a follow-up session:
.RS
\f(CRqlchroot \-k /mnt /usr/bin/amu \-U\fR
.RE

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR chroot (1),
.BR mount (8),
.BR genfstab (8),
.BR amu (8)

